# Versioning

Semver in `VERSION` (one line, `X.Y.Z`). The Makefile, the deb build and the
release workflow read it, and the release workflow refuses a tag that does
not match it. Bump it with every shipped change, once per chat session.

Keep three places in sync:

- `VERSION`
- `README.md` badge on line 3: `![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-X.Y.Z-brightgreen)`
- `CHANGELOG.md`: a new section at the top

| Bump | When |
| --- | --- |
| patch | fix, refactor, docs, CI |
| minor | a new flag, action, wizard step or installer option |
| major | a breaking change: a flag removed or renamed, or files in another place (see AGENTS.md rule 1) |

Changelog format: `### vX.Y.Z (YYYY-MM-DD)`, `*` bullets, a bolded area
ending with a colon, present tense, what the user notices. Areas: `CLI:`,
`Installer:`, `Sites:`, `Fix:`, `Docs:`, `Repo:`. No em dashes. The release
notes are the tag's section, and webtimeless.cloud's changelog reads the
same file.
